From 224099d21f6ceec234f0a43f1d997f0be1e1f7c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jaewun <jaewun@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 01:20:00 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] thermal: qcom: tsens: skip AYN Thor uplow wake IRQs

On AYN Thor, the SM8550 TSENS uplow/passive threshold IRQ is not a useful
system wake source and can immediately wake the system from suspend.

Keep normal TSENS interrupt handling active and keep critical TSENS wake
enabled. Only skip enable_irq_wake() for the ordinary "uplow" TSENS IRQs on
ayn,thor.

[Thorch rebase: on Linux 7.2 the wake IRQ is armed in
 tsens_suspend_common()/tsens_resume_common() using the uplow_irq that
 tsens_register_irq() only stores now.  Guard both the enable and the
 symmetric disable so the resume path does not warn on a wake source that
 was never armed.]

Signed-off-by: jaewun <jaewun@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c b/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c
index 6e3714eca..4e1cce436 100644
--- a/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c
@@ -1297,7 +1297,9 @@ int tsens_suspend_common(struct tsens_priv *priv)
 	if (priv->feat->combo_int)
 		enable_irq_wake(priv->combined_irq);
 	else {
-		enable_irq_wake(priv->uplow_irq);
+		/* The uplow threshold IRQ is a noisy non-wakeup source on AYN Thor. */
+		if (!of_machine_is_compatible("ayn,thor"))
+			enable_irq_wake(priv->uplow_irq);
 		if (priv->feat->crit_int)
 			enable_irq_wake(priv->crit_irq);
 	}
@@ -1316,7 +1318,9 @@ int tsens_resume_common(struct tsens_priv *priv)
 	if (priv->feat->combo_int)
 		disable_irq_wake(priv->combined_irq);
 	else {
-		disable_irq_wake(priv->uplow_irq);
+		/* Only woke the uplow IRQ if it was armed as a wake source. */
+		if (!of_machine_is_compatible("ayn,thor"))
+			disable_irq_wake(priv->uplow_irq);
 		if (priv->feat->crit_int)
 			disable_irq_wake(priv->crit_irq);
 	}
